    <bpmn:process id="W_W819" name="W819. Vendor Quality Incoming Inspection Failure &amp; Material Review Board (MRB)" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Quality inspection failure at DC receiving per W681 or store receiving per W666
Frequency: Per failure (continuous review; ~7–10/day chain-wide); ~200–300 quality failures per month across 4 DCs and 200 stores (per W110; ~30–50 escalate to MRB disposition)
Volume: ~200–300 failures/month (per W110); ~30–50 escalate to MRB disposition
Owner: Quality Assurance Analyst
Participants: QA Analyst, DC Receiving Supervisor, Procurement Analyst, Department Manager, Vendor
Source: workflow W819 — Vendor Quality Incoming Inspection Failure &amp; Material Review Board (MRB)</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W819_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W819_Lane1" name="DC Receiving Inspector">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W819_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W819_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W819_Lane2" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W819_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W819_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W819_Lane3" name="QA Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W819_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W819_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W819_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W819_Task15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W819_Task16</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W819_Lane4" name="MRB Panel">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W819_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W819_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W819_End17</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W819_Start6" name="Quality inspection failure at DC receiving per W681 or store receiving per W666">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W819_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W819_Task7" name="DC Receiving Inspector identifies quality failure">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: DC Receiving Inspector identifies quality failure during inspection per W681: documents defect type, severity, affected quantity, photo evidence
Responsible (R): DC Receiving Inspector
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 10-20 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W819_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W819_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W819_Task8" name="System creates quality hold">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: System creates quality hold: quarantined inventory flagged, PO receipt blocked per W2
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): DC Receiving Supervisor
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W819_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W819_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W819_Task9" name="QA Analyst performs root cause classification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: QA Analyst performs root cause classification: (a) critical safety defect (e.g., electrical product wiring) — immediate full reject, (b) major quality defect (dimensional, functional) — MRB review required, (c) minor cosmetic defect — accept with concession decision at DC level
Responsible (R): QA Analyst
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 15-30 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W819_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W819_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W819_Task10" name="For critical safety defects">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: For critical safety defects: automatic full reject → RTV per W88; vendor CAPA per W110; product recall risk assessment per W29
Responsible (R): QA Analyst
Accountable (A): Procurement Manager
Duration: 30-60 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W819_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W819_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W819_Task11" name="For major defects">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: For major defects: QA Analyst convenes MRB within 48 hours — Procurement Analyst, DC Supervisor, category-relevant Department Manager
Responsible (R): QA Analyst
Accountable (A): Department Manager
Duration: Scheduling: 15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W819_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W819_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W819_Task12" name="MRB evaluates">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: MRB evaluates: (a) vendor negotiation for price concession vs. RTV cost, (b) store demand urgency (can stores wait for replacement?), (c) seasonal timing (near promo period?), (d) rework feasibility and cost, (e) customer impact of stock-out
Responsible (R): MRB Panel (QA, Procurement, DC, Dept Mgr)
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 1-2 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W819_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W819_Flow26</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W819_Task13" name="MRB disposition decision">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: MRB disposition decision: (a) Return to Vendor (RTV per W88), (b) Accept with Concession (price reduction negotiated, debit memo per W770), (c) Rework and Accept (vendor pays rework cost), (d) Scrap (write-off per W92 inventory adjustment)
Responsible (R): MRB Panel
Accountable (A): Procurement Manager
Duration: 15-30 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W819_Flow26</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W819_Flow27</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W819_Task14" name="System executes disposition">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: System executes disposition: updates inventory status, triggers vendor debit memo per W770 if applicable, adjusts PO line if partial delivery
Responsible (R): System / QA Analyst
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 15-30 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W819_Flow27</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W819_Flow28</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W819_Task15" name="QA Analyst creates vendor quality incident record">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 9: QA Analyst creates vendor quality incident record per W110 for CAPA tracking
Responsible (R): QA Analyst
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W819_Flow28</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W819_Flow29</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W819_Task16" name="Monthly quality failure analytics">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 10: Monthly quality failure analytics: failure rate by vendor, by category, by defect type; MRB disposition distribution; vendor CAPA completion rate
Responsible (R): QA Analyst
Accountable (A): Quality Assurance Manager
Duration: 3 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W819_Flow29</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W819_Flow30</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W819_End17" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W819_Flow30</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W819_Annotation18">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-246 (ensure controlled execution — Vendor Sourcing &amp; Onboarding (PA-03.1).) | - operational: Quality Assurance Analyst review and approval gate
Owner: Quality Assurance Analyst</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W819_Assoc19" sourceRef="W819_Annotation18" targetRef="W819_Start6" associationDirection="None" />
