    <bpmn:process id="W_W995" name="W995. Vendor Consignment Inventory Aging Analysis &amp; Automatic Markdown Trigger" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Monthly consignment inventory aging analysis run (scheduled); or individual SKU aging threshold breach
Frequency: Monthly analysis; continuous threshold monitoring
Volume: ~300 consignment SKUs from ~15–25 consignment vendors; ~30–50 SKUs flagged for markdown action per month
Owner: Category Manager
Participants: Buyer, Merchandising Planner, Vendor (consignment partner), Store Operations
Source: workflow W995 — Vendor Consignment Inventory Aging Analysis &amp; Automatic Markdown Trigger</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W995_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W995_Lane1" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W995_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W995_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W995_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W995_Lane2" name="Buyer">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W995_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W995_Lane3" name="Category Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W995_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W995_Lane4" name="Finance Department">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W995_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W995_End12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W995_Start6" name="Monthly consignment inventory aging analysis run (scheduled); or individual SKU aging…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W995_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W995_Task7" name="Monthly Consignment Inventory Aging Report Generation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Monthly Consignment Inventory Aging Report Generation: System generates aging analysis for all consignment SKUs: (a) age buckets — 0–30 days (fresh), 31–60 days (aging), 61–90 days (slow), 91–180 days (very slow), 181–365 days (stale), &gt;365 days (dead stock); (b) per SKU: date of receipt, total units received, units sold, units remaining, days since receipt, sell-through rate (%); (c) per vendor: total consignment inventory value by age bucket, number of SKUs in each bucket, shelf space occupied (sqm) by stale/dead consignment stock; (d) exception list: SKUs breaching 60-day, 90-day, and 180-day thresholds; (e) system generates report and distributes to Category Manager and Buyer via email/dashboard
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: Automated (5 min to review)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W995_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W995_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W995_Task8" name="Aging Threshold Escalation &amp; Markdown Trigger">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Aging Threshold Escalation &amp; Markdown Trigger: System automatically triggers actions based on aging thresholds: (a) 61–90 days (Yellow Alert): System sends automated notification to Buyer and Vendor with SKU details, aging data, and sell-through rate; Buyer contacts vendor to discuss: promotional markdown (vendor-funded per W161), improved in-store positioning, or vendor-initiated stock rotation; no mandatory action yet — collaborative approach; (b) 91–180 days (Orange Alert): System triggers mandatory vendor notification with 14-day response deadline; Buyer and Category Manager review; options: (i) vendor-funded markdown of 15–25% off SRP with vendor absorbing margin loss; (ii) vendor repatriates stock (at vendor&#x27;s logistics cost); (iii) BuildRight converts consignment to owned stock at negotiated discount (50–70% of original cost) and applies W93 markdown; vendor must respond within 14 days or option (iii) auto-activates; (c) &gt;180 days (Red Alert): System auto-triggers markdown at 30% off SRP if vendor did not respond to Orange Alert; markdown cost charged to vendor account per consignment agreement terms; unsold units after 30-day markdown period: vendor must repatriate within 14 days or BuildRight disposes per W91 (salvage/scrap) with vendor bearing disposal cost
Responsible (R): System / Buyer
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 1–2 hours/month (escalation handling)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W995_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W995_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W995_Task9" name="Vendor Communication &amp; Resolution">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Vendor Communication &amp; Resolution: Buyer contacts vendor per escalation tier: (a) presents aging data and sell-through analysis; (b) discusses root causes — pricing too high, product not competitive, poor in-store visibility, wrong store cluster allocation; (c) negotiates resolution — promotional pricing, stock swap (replace slow SKU with faster variant), improved display, or stock return; (d) records resolution in vendor collaboration portal per W357 (vendor portal); (e) for vendors with recurring aging issues (≥3 SKUs in Orange/Red per quarter): escalates to Category Manager for consignment agreement review and potential shelf space reallocation
Responsible (R): Buyer / Category Manager
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 30–60 min per vendor</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W995_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W995_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W995_Task10" name="Markdown Execution &amp; POS Update">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Markdown Execution &amp; POS Update: For agreed markdowns: (a) Category Manager approves markdown percentage per W93 markdown authorization; (b) system updates SRP across all stores with affected consignment SKUs; (c) POS system reflects new price within 1 hour per real-time event streaming; (d) ecommerce platform price updated per ECOM-002; (e) shelf labels reprinted and applied per W63; (f) markdown tracked separately in consignment settlement report for vendor deduction during next reconciliation per W23; (g) system monitors sell-through rate post-markdown at weekly intervals
Responsible (R): Category Manager / Store Operations
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 30–60 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W995_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W995_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W995_Task11" name="Consignment Settlement Adjustment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Consignment Settlement Adjustment: During monthly consignment settlement per W23: (a) system calculates: units sold × original agreed price (vendor revenue), minus markdown cost (charged to vendor per consignment agreement), minus any repatriation logistics cost; (b) settlement report emailed to vendor per W357; (c) vendor disputes resolved per vendor dispute resolution per W359; (d) payment to vendor net of markdown charges per standard payment terms
Responsible (R): Finance Department / Buyer
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: Included in monthly settlement cycle</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W995_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W995_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W995_End12" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W995_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W995_Annotation13">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-246 (ensure controlled execution — Vendor Sourcing &amp; Onboarding (PA-03.1).) | - operational: consignment aging report reconciled to cycle-count data monthly before escalation actions are triggered
Owner: Category Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W995_Assoc14" sourceRef="W995_Annotation13" targetRef="W995_Start6" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W995_Flow15" sourceRef="W995_Start6" targetRef="W995_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W995_Flow16" sourceRef="W995_Task7" targetRef="W995_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W995_Flow17" sourceRef="W995_Task8" targetRef="W995_Task9" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W995_Flow18" sourceRef="W995_Task9" targetRef="W995_Task10" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W995_Flow19" sourceRef="W995_Task10" targetRef="W995_Task11" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W995_Flow20" sourceRef="W995_Task11" targetRef="W995_End12" />
    </bpmn:process>
    <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="W995_diag">
      <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="W995_plane" bpmnElement="W_W995">
