    <bpmn:process id="W_W1002" name="W1002. Vendor Product Sampling &amp; Test Batch Inventory Lifecycle Management" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Vendor submits new product sample for BuildRight evaluation; or Buyer requests sample from vendor for evaluation
Frequency: ~200–300 new product samples/year chain-wide; ~20–30 active test batches at any time
Volume: 1 product per sample submission; test batches of 50–500 units per SKU
Owner: Category Manager
Participants: Buyer, Quality Assurance (QA), Store Operations (test store), Vendor, Merchandising Planner
Source: workflow W1002 — Vendor Product Sampling &amp; Test Batch Inventory Lifecycle Management</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1002_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1002_Lane1" name="Buyer">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1002_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1002_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1002_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1002_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1002_Lane2" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1002_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1002_Lane3" name="Category Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1002_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1002_End11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1002_Start5" name="Vendor submits new product sample for BuildRight evaluation; or Buyer requests sample…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1002_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1002_Task6" name="Sample Submission &amp; Registration">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Sample Submission &amp; Registration: Vendor submits product sample via: (a) in-person delivery to Buyer at HQ or store visit; (b) shipment to HQ merchandising department; (c) upload via vendor portal per W357 (product images, specifications, pricing, certifications); Buyer registers sample in system: (a) product description, category, vendor, country of origin; (b) proposed SRP, cost, margin; (c) product certifications (DTI-BPS ICC/SOC per W447, FDA LTO per W479 if applicable); (d) competitive positioning vs. existing assortment; (e) sample assigned unique Sample ID and status: &quot;Received — Pending Evaluation&quot;
Responsible (R): Buyer / Vendor
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 15–20 min per sample</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1002_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1002_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1002_Task7" name="Quality &amp; Commercial Evaluation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Quality &amp; Commercial Evaluation: Buyer and QA evaluate sample: (a) Quality assessment: material quality, finish, durability, compliance with PH standards (DTI-BPS, DENR, FDA as applicable per W447, W477, W479); physical testing — drop test, water resistance (for outdoor products), color fastness, dimensional accuracy; (b) Commercial assessment: SRP competitiveness vs. existing assortment and competitor pricing per W130; estimated demand (based on category trends, customer requests, seasonal relevance); margin analysis (target gross margin 28–32%); vendor reliability (on-time delivery, quality history per W44); (c) Packaging assessment: packaging integrity for Philippine logistics conditions (humidity, rough handling, stacking in DC); labeling compliance (Filipino/English language, DTI-mandated information per Consumer Act RA 7394); (d) evaluation score: Quality (40%), Commercial Viability (40%), Packaging (20%); minimum score ≥70/100 to proceed to test batch
Responsible (R): Buyer / QA
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 1–2 hours per sample</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1002_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1002_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1002_Task8" name="Test Batch Procurement &amp; Deployment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Test Batch Procurement &amp; Deployment: If sample passes evaluation (score ≥70): (a) Buyer orders test batch from vendor — 50–500 units depending on category and price point; smaller quantities for high-value items (power tools, appliances), larger for consumables (paint, adhesives); (b) test batch received at DC per W3 with special &quot;Test Batch&quot; inventory tag; (c) Merchandising Planner selects 3–5 pilot stores based on: store cluster match (customer demographic fit per W299 assortment matrix), store manager capability (willing to actively promote test product), geographic diversity (different regions for market feedback); (d) test batch distributed to pilot stores via W4 replenishment; (e) system tracks test batch inventory separately from regular inventory with &quot;Test Batch&quot; flag
Responsible (R): Buyer / Merchandising Planner / Supply Chain Planner
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 2–3 hours per test batch</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1002_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1002_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1002_Task9" name="Test Period Monitoring (60–90 days)">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Test Period Monitoring (60–90 days): During test period: (a) system tracks sell-through rate per test store — weekly sell-through vs. target (minimum 60% sell-through in 90 days for approval); (b) Store Manager at pilot stores provides weekly feedback — customer reaction, price sensitivity, display effectiveness, product issues; (c) Category Manager conducts mid-test review at 45 days — if sell-through &lt;30% at midpoint: early termination considered, remaining stock clearance-priced per W93; if sell-through &gt;50% at midpoint: consider accelerating rollout; (d) customer feedback collected per W87 — post-purchase survey for test batch purchasers; (e) system generates weekly test batch performance dashboard for Category Manager review
Responsible (R): System / Store Manager / Category Manager
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 30 min/week per active test batch</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1002_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1002_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1002_Task10" name="Test Batch Disposition &amp; Rollout Decision">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Test Batch Disposition &amp; Rollout Decision: At end of test period: (a) Approve for rollout (sell-through ≥60%): Category Manager approves SKU for chain-wide assortment per W64; system creates regular SKU master per W252; Buyer negotiates chain-wide purchase order per W2 with volume pricing; Merchandising Planner allocates to all relevant store clusters per W299; (b) Conditional approval (sell-through 40–60%): Category Manager approves with modifications — adjusted pricing, different store clusters, improved packaging; limited rollout to top-performing test stores only; re-test with modifications; (c) Reject (sell-through &lt;40%): Category Manager rejects SKU; remaining test batch inventory dispositioned — return to vendor per W88 (if vendor accepts returns); clearance markdown per W93 (if vendor does not accept return); write-off per W91 if unsellable; vendor notified of rejection reason via vendor portal per W357; (d) all test batch financial results (purchase cost, revenue, margin, disposition cost) recorded for vendor performance tracking per W44
Responsible (R): Category Manager / Buyer / Merchandising Planner
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 1–2 hours per disposition decision</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1002_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1002_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1002_End11" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1002_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1002_Annotation12">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-246 (ensure controlled execution — Vendor Sourcing &amp; Onboarding (PA-03.1).) | - operational: Category Manager review and approval gate
Owner: Category Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1002_Assoc13" sourceRef="W1002_Annotation12" targetRef="W1002_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1002_Flow14" sourceRef="W1002_Start5" targetRef="W1002_Task6" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1002_Flow15" sourceRef="W1002_Task6" targetRef="W1002_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1002_Flow16" sourceRef="W1002_Task7" targetRef="W1002_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1002_Flow17" sourceRef="W1002_Task8" targetRef="W1002_Task9" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1002_Flow18" sourceRef="W1002_Task9" targetRef="W1002_Task10" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1002_Flow19" sourceRef="W1002_Task10" targetRef="W1002_End11" />
    </bpmn:process>
