    <bpmn:process id="W_W1035" name="W1035. Store-Level Return-to-Vendor (RTV) Consolidation &amp; Batch Shipping Processing" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Accumulated RTV items at store reach minimum batch quantity or scheduled monthly RTV consolidation date
Frequency: Monthly per store (scheduled); ad-hoc for high-value or urgent RTV items
Volume: ~5–20 RTV items per store per month; ~1,000–4,500 RTV items chain-wide/month (per W88&#x27;s shipment/line counts)
Owner: Department Supervisor
Participants: Stock Associate, Receiving Clerk, Procurement Specialist, Vendor, AP Clerk
Source: workflow W1035 — Store-Level Return-to-Vendor (RTV) Consolidation &amp; Batch Shipping Processing</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1035_LaneSet6">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1035_Lane1" name="Stock Associates">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1035_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1035_Start7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1035_Lane2" name="Department Supervisor">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1035_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1035_Lane3" name="Receiving Clerk">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1035_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1035_Lane4" name="AP Clerk">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1035_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1035_Lane5" name="Procurement Specialist">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1035_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1035_End13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1035_Start7" name="Accumulated RTV items at store reach minimum batch quantity or scheduled monthly RTV…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1035_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1035_Task8" name="RTV Quarantine Accumulation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: RTV Quarantine Accumulation: Throughout the month, Stock Associates place RTV-eligible items in designated quarantine area: (a) items are already authorized for RTV per W88 (RTV Processing) — system has RTV authorization number, vendor approval, and expected credit amount; (b) each item scanned into quarantine with: RTV authorization number, SKU, quantity, defect code, vendor code; (c) system tracks quarantine inventory separately from active stock (unavailable for sale); (d) items stored organized by vendor to facilitate batch packing; (e) hazardous RTV items (paint, chemicals) stored per W236 (Hazmat Storage) in separate hazmat quarantine area; (f) system sends alert to Department Supervisor when quarantine count reaches 30+ items or 60% of quarantine area capacity — trigger early consolidation
Responsible (R): Stock Associates
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 5 min per item (ongoing)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1035_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1035_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1035_Task9" name="Monthly Consolidation &amp; Sort">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Monthly Consolidation &amp; Sort: On scheduled RTV consolidation day (store-specific date within last week of month): (a) Department Supervisor and Stock Associates sort all quarantine items by vendor: (i) group items by vendor code, (ii) verify each item matches an active RTV authorization (no unauthorized items in batch), (iii) verify physical item matches system record (SKU, quantity, condition), (iv) remove items with expired RTV authorizations (&gt; 90 days old, vendor may no longer accept — route to store-level write-off per W220); (b) pack items by vendor in cardboard boxes or pallets: (i) label each package with vendor name, vendor code, RTV authorization numbers included, total items, and total expected credit value; (ii) fragile items (tiles, glass, electrical fixtures) packed with bubble wrap/foam protection to prevent further damage in transit; (iii) hazmat items (paint, chemicals) packed per hazmat shipping requirements per W699; (c) system generates consolidated RTV shipping manifest per vendor with item detail and expected credit summary
Responsible (R): Department Supervisor / Stock Associates
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 60–120 min/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1035_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1035_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1035_Task10" name="DC Consolidation Shipping">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: DC Consolidation Shipping: Store ships RTV batches to assigned DC via return leg of next DC delivery truck: (a) Receiving Clerk coordinates with DC dispatch per W106 — RTV items loaded onto returning truck (normally empty on DC-to-store leg); (b) shipping manifest (step 2c) provided to truck driver; (c) store scans items out of quarantine with &quot;shipped to DC&quot; status; (d) system updates inventory: items no longer at store, in-transit to DC; (e) DC Receiving Supervisor receives RTV shipment: verifies manifest against physical packages, logs receipt in system; (f) DC consolidates RTV items from multiple stores by vendor: all items for Vendor A from stores in the DC&#x27;s region are combined into a single vendor shipment; (g) DC notifies vendors per W866 (Vendor Portal) that RTV shipment is ready for pickup or provides estimated ship date for carrier dispatch
Responsible (R): Receiving Clerk / DC Receiving Supervisor
Accountable (A): DC Operations Manager
Duration: 15–30 min per store (shipping); 2–4 hours/week at DC (consolidation)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1035_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1035_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1035_Task11" name="Vendor Credit Reconciliation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Vendor Credit Reconciliation: After vendor receives and inspects RTV shipment: (a) vendor issues credit note per agreed terms (typically within 30 days of receipt); (b) AP Clerk matches vendor credit note against RTV shipping manifest: (i) verify credit amount matches expected credit per RTV authorization; (ii) if vendor issues partial credit (claims some items were not defective or were damaged in transit), dispute resolution per W244 (Vendor Invoice Dispute); (iii) if vendor denies credit entirely, escalate to Procurement Specialist for resolution; (c) upon credit match: system posts credit to AP vendor account, reducing amount owed to vendor on next payment run per W556; (d) AP Clerk reconciles RTV credits monthly: total credits expected vs. credits received; unreconciled items &gt; 60 days escalated to Procurement Specialist
Responsible (R): AP Clerk / Procurement Specialist
Accountable (A): Finance Controller
Duration: 15–30 min per vendor credit</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1035_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1035_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1035_Task12" name="RTV Analytics &amp; Vendor Quality Feedback">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: RTV Analytics &amp; Vendor Quality Feedback: Monthly: (a) system generates RTV analytics: (i) RTV volume by vendor, by category, by defect reason code; (ii) RTV rate as % of total purchases per vendor (target: &lt; 2%); (iii) RTV credit recovery rate (credits received ÷ credits expected); (b) vendors with RTV rate &gt; 5% for 3 consecutive months: Buyer escalates per W110 (Supplier Quality &amp; CAPA); (c) defect reason analysis: are RTVs caused by vendor quality issues (defective products), transit damage (inadequate packaging), or customer misuse (improper installation); root cause analysis feeds back into receiving inspection criteria per W681 (DC Quality Control) and W666 (Store-Level Receiving QC); (d) RTV shipping cost analysis: total RTV logistics cost vs. credit recovered — if logistics cost exceeds credit value, consider disposing locally per W91 instead of returning to vendor
Responsible (R): Procurement Specialist / Category Manager
Accountable (A): VP Supply Chain
Duration: 2–4 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1035_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1035_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1035_End13" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1035_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1035_Annotation14">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-246 (ensure controlled execution — Vendor Sourcing &amp; Onboarding (PA-03.1).) | - operational: Department Supervisor review and approval gate; operational: periodic reconciliation against source documents
Owner: Department Supervisor</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1035_Assoc15" sourceRef="W1035_Annotation14" targetRef="W1035_Start7" associationDirection="None" />
