    <bpmn:process id="W_W1038" name="W1038. Vendor Catalog Synchronization &amp; Product Information Quality Audit" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Monthly scheduled audit; also triggered by product data quality score drop or vendor catalog update notification
Frequency: Monthly audit × top 100 vendors (by purchase volume); quarterly for remaining vendors
Volume: ~10,000–12,000 SKU data records audited per month (top-10K prioritization per the pain point)
Owner: Product Content Manager
Participants: Vendor (catalog data provider), Category Manager, Ecommerce Content Specialist, IT Data Quality Analyst
Source: workflow W1038 — Vendor Catalog Synchronization &amp; Product Information Quality Audit</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1038_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1038_Lane1" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1038_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1038_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1038_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1038_Lane2" name="Product Content Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1038_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1038_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1038_Lane3" name="Ecommerce Content Specialist">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1038_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1038_End11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1038_Start5" name="Monthly scheduled audit; also triggered by product data quality score drop or vendor…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1038_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1038_Task6" name="Automated Data Quality Scoring">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Automated Data Quality Scoring: System automatically scores each SKU record daily on data quality dimensions: (a) Completeness (0–100): % of mandatory fields populated: product name, description, dimensions (L×W×H), weight, material, color/finish, brand, country of origin, barcode/GTIN (W311), images (minimum 1 main + 2 detail), compliance certifications; (b) Accuracy (0–100): data validation rules — dimensions within category range (e.g., a &quot;nail&quot; shouldn&#x27;t have dimensions of 2m), weight matches category norms, barcode format valid (EAN-13, UPC-A), price within ±50% of category average; (c) Freshness (0–100): days since last vendor update — score decays over time (100 if updated within 30 days, 0 if &gt; 365 days); (d) Richness (0–100): presence of enhanced content: 360° images, installation guides, how-to videos, customer reviews, comparison data; (e) overall SKU data quality score = weighted average (Completeness 40% + Accuracy 30% + Freshness 20% + Richness 10%); (f) system flags SKUs scoring &lt; 70 for audit
Responsible (R): System (Data Quality Engine)
Accountable (A): Product Content Manager
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1038_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1038_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1038_Task7" name="Monthly Vendor Catalog Pull &amp; Delta Detection">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Monthly Vendor Catalog Pull &amp; Delta Detection: Monthly (1st of each month): (a) system pulls latest catalog data from vendor via: (i) vendor portal (W868) self-service data upload, (ii) EDI/API integration (for top 20 vendors with automated catalog feeds), (iii) email/shared folder import (for small vendors providing Excel/PDF catalogs); (b) system compares vendor catalog data against current PIM data: (i) detect changes: new products, discontinued products (flagged per W1026), modified specifications, updated images, new compliance documents; (ii) detect gaps: vendor catalog has data that BuildRight PIM is missing; (iii) detect conflicts: vendor catalog data contradicts BuildRight PIM data (e.g., vendor says weight is 5 kg, PIM says 3 kg); (c) system generates delta report per vendor with all changes, gaps, and conflicts
Responsible (R): System / IT Data Quality Analyst
Accountable (A): Product Content Manager
Duration: Automated (system); 2–3 hours/week (analyst review)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1038_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1038_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1038_Task8" name="Data Quality Audit &amp; Resolution">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Data Quality Audit &amp; Resolution: Product Content Manager reviews flagged SKUs (score &lt; 70) and delta report: (a) Missing data: request missing information from vendor via vendor portal ticket (W869); set 15-business-day response SLA; if vendor doesn&#x27;t respond, Product Content Manager sources data from manufacturer website, product packaging photos, or physical product measurement; (b) Inaccurate data: verify against authoritative source — manufacturer datasheet, physical product measurement, or third-party product database; correct PIM record with source documentation; (c) Conflicts: if vendor catalog contradicts PIM, physical verification required — Department Supervisor at a designated store measures/weighs the actual product and provides photo confirmation; PIM updated based on physical verification; (d) Stale data: flag for vendor refresh request; if vendor doesn&#x27;t update within 60 days, Product Content Manager updates based on best available information with &quot;unverified&quot; flag; (e) all changes logged in PIM audit trail per W686 (Document Approval Routing)
Responsible (R): Product Content Manager / Ecommerce Content Specialist
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 20–30 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1038_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1038_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1038_Task9" name="Ecommerce Catalog Impact Assessment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Ecommerce Catalog Impact Assessment: For data quality issues affecting ecommerce: (a) Ecommerce Content Specialist reviews flagged SKUs with customer-facing impact: incorrect dimensions (customer orders wrong size product), missing images (reduces conversion rate by 30–50%), incorrect specifications (causes returns); (b) priority resolution: ecommerce-impacting data issues resolved within 48 hours; (c) if data issue cannot be resolved quickly: ecommerce listing temporarily updated with disclaimer &quot;Specifications being verified. Contact store for confirmed details.&quot;; (d) system tracks ecommerce conversion rate by SKU data quality score — quantify the revenue impact of data quality to justify investment in data governance per W709
Responsible (R): Ecommerce Content Specialist
Accountable (A): Ecommerce Operations Manager
Duration: 8–10 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1038_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1038_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1038_Task10" name="Quarterly Vendor Data Quality Scorecard &amp; Improvement Program">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Quarterly Vendor Data Quality Scorecard &amp; Improvement Program: Quarterly: (a) Product Content Manager generates vendor data quality scorecard per W871 (Supplier Scorecard Portal Publication): (i) average SKU data quality score per vendor, (ii) completeness rate, accuracy rate, freshness rate per vendor, (iii) comparison vs. vendor peer average; (b) publish scorecard on vendor portal per W871 — vendors see their data quality score and how they compare to peers; (c) vendors with score &lt; 60 for 2 consecutive quarters: placed on data quality improvement plan with specific requirements (e.g., &quot;provide images for all SKUs within 60 days&quot;); (d) vendors with score &gt; 90 recognized as &quot;Data Quality Partners&quot; — their catalog updates receive expedited processing; (e) aggregate data quality metrics reported to VP Merchandising and CIO for investment planning
Responsible (R): Product Content Manager
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 4–6 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1038_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1038_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1038_End11" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1038_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1038_Annotation12">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-246 (ensure controlled execution — Vendor Sourcing &amp; Onboarding (PA-03.1).) | - operational: Product Content Manager review and approval gate
Owner: Product Content Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1038_Assoc13" sourceRef="W1038_Annotation12" targetRef="W1038_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
