    <bpmn:process id="W_W1087" name="W1087. Store-Level Power Tool Brand Ambassador &amp; Vendor Demo Day Event Management" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Vendor requests an in-store demo day event, or Store Manager schedules a monthly demo day calendar per the merchandising promotional plan
Frequency: 2–4 vendor demo events per store per month (power tool vendors: Bosch, Makita, DeWalt, Milwaukee, Ryobi, Crown, Ingco, total tools, etc.)
Volume: 1 event per trigger (each event features 1–3 tool brands, lasts 4–8 hours)
Owner: Store Manager
Participants: Department Supervisor (Tools/Hardware), Vendor Brand Ambassador, Sales Associates (Tools Section), Customers, Merchandising Category Manager (HQ)
Source: workflow W1087 — Store-Level Power Tool Brand Ambassador &amp; Vendor Demo Day Event Management</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1087_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1087_Lane1" name="Category Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1087_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1087_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1087_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1087_Lane2" name="Department Supervisor">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1087_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1087_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1087_Lane3" name="Vendor Brand Ambassador">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1087_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1087_End11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1087_Start5" name="Vendor requests an in-store demo day event, or Store Manager schedules a monthly demo day…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1087_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1087_Task6" name="Demo Day Calendar Planning &amp; Vendor Coordination">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Demo Day Calendar Planning &amp; Vendor Coordination: (a) Merchandising Category Manager (HQ) creates quarterly demo day calendar: allocates dates, time slots, and store clusters to each participating vendor; ensures no scheduling conflicts between competing brands on the same date at the same store; (b) Category Manager sends calendar to vendors 60 days in advance with: store assignment, date, time slot (morning: 9AM–12PM, afternoon: 1PM–5PM, or full-day), floor space allocation (typically 3m × 3m in the tools section or at the store entrance), and electrical power availability; (c) vendor confirms participation and provides: brand ambassador name(s), tool models to be demonstrated, special demo-day pricing/promotions, freebie/giveaway items, and marketing materials (banners, brochures, sample boards); (d) Store Manager approves the calendar and assigns Department Supervisor as event coordinator
Responsible (R): Category Manager (HQ) / Vendor
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: Quarterly planning: 4–6 hrs; Per-event coordination: 30 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1087_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1087_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1087_Task7" name="Pre-Event Store Preparation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Pre-Event Store Preparation: (a) Department Supervisor prepares demo area: clears 3m × 3m space in tools section or store entrance, sets up demo table/workbench, ensures adequate electrical outlets (220V, dedicated circuit for each tool brand to avoid tripping), sets up safety barriers (demo area must be separated from customer walkway by at least 1 meter), positions fire extinguisher per W1051; (b) Supervisor sets up vendor branding: positions vendor banners, product displays, and marketing materials per vendor&#x27;s layout instructions; (c) Supervisor verifies demo tool inventory: confirms all tools to be demonstrated are in stock with sufficient quantities for anticipated demo-day sales; if stock is low, triggers emergency replenishment per W60 (emergency procurement) or W4B (store-initiated replenishment); (d) Store Manager briefs Sales Associates on demo day objectives, target sales, and special promotions; (e) system generates demo-day sales target for each participating vendor based on historical demo-day performance
Responsible (R): Department Supervisor
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 2–3 hrs per event (day before)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1087_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1087_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1087_Task8" name="Live Demo Day Execution">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Live Demo Day Execution: (a) Vendor Brand Ambassador arrives 30 minutes before event start for setup and tool preparation; (b) Department Supervisor conducts safety briefing with Ambassador: PPE requirements (safety goggles per demo, no loose clothing), fire extinguisher location, emergency stop procedures, maximum noise tolerance (no continuous operation &gt;5 minutes to avoid disturbing other customers); (c) Ambassador conducts live tool demonstrations: drilling (concrete block, wood, metal), cutting (circular saw on plywood, angle grinder on rebar), sanding, impact driving, rotary hammering; (d) Sales Associates support by: answering pricing questions, checking inventory availability on handheld, processing demo-day sales at dedicated mPOS terminal per W206, directing interested customers to full product selection; (e) system tracks real-time demo-day sales against target; (f) Store Manager monitors crowd flow and safety compliance; (g) Ambassador offers demo-day-only promotions: buy-drill-get-free-bit-set, extended 2-year warranty registration, free tool bag with purchase above PHP 5,000; (h) customer purchases processed at POS with demo-day promotional pricing applied automatically via W13 (promotions &amp; pricing execution)
Responsible (R): Vendor Brand Ambassador / Sales Associates
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 4–8 hrs per event</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1087_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1087_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1087_Task9" name="Post-Event Sales Reconciliation &amp; Vendor Reporting">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Post-Event Sales Reconciliation &amp; Vendor Reporting: (a) system generates demo-day sales report: units sold by SKU, revenue, demo-day promotional discount amounts, conversion rate (units sold ÷ unique customer interactions estimated by Ambassador), and comparison to target; (b) Department Supervisor conducts demo area cleanup: stores demo tools, disassembles vendor branding, restores floor space to normal planogram per W314; (c) vendor promotional costs reconciled: vendor-funded discounts and freebies are charged back to vendor per W513 (vendor-funded promotional activity); (d) demo-day sales report sent to Category Manager (HQ) and vendor within 24 hours; (e) Store Manager files event documentation: attendance log, safety incident report (if any), customer feedback, photos for marketing per W142 (social media management)
Responsible (R): Department Supervisor / System
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 1–2 hrs post-event</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1087_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1087_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1087_Task10" name="Quarterly Demo Day Program Performance Review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Quarterly Demo Day Program Performance Review: (a) Category Manager (HQ) compiles quarterly demo day program results: total events, total revenue, vendor participation rate, average revenue per event, top-performing brands and stores, customer satisfaction scores; (b) Category Manager reviews vendor performance: brand ambassador professionalism, promotional investment, sales conversion rate, customer engagement quality; (c) program adjustments: increase frequency for high-performing vendors, reduce or replace underperforming vendors, adjust store assignments based on regional tool preferences; (d) results presented in quarterly vendor business review per W155 (vendor strategic collaboration &amp; JBP)
Responsible (R): Category Manager (HQ)
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 3–4 hrs per quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1087_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1087_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1087_End11" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1087_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1087_Annotation12">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-246 (ensure controlled execution — Vendor Sourcing &amp; Onboarding (PA-03.1).) | - operational: Store Manager review and approval gate; operational: periodic reconciliation against source documents
Owner: Store Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1087_Assoc13" sourceRef="W1087_Annotation12" targetRef="W1087_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1087_Flow14" sourceRef="W1087_Start5" targetRef="W1087_Task6" />
