    <bpmn:process id="W_W1099" name="W1099. Store-Level Vendor-Sponsored Product Training Academy &amp; Staff Certification Program" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Vendor proposes a structured multi-week product training program for BuildRight staff, or Category Manager identifies a knowledge gap in a specific product category requiring vendor-led certification
Frequency: ~200–300 staff certification events/year across all stores (averaging 1–1.5 certifications per store per year)
Volume: 5–15 staff per certification cohort per store
Owner: Store Manager
Participants: Department Supervisors, Sales Associates (relevant section), Vendor Training Specialist, HR Training Coordinator, Category Manager
Source: workflow W1099 — Store-Level Vendor-Sponsored Product Training Academy &amp; Staff Certification Program</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1099_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1099_Lane1" name="Category Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1099_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1099_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1099_Lane2" name="Store Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1099_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1099_Lane3" name="Vendor Training Specialist">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1099_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1099_Lane4" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1099_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1099_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1099_End12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1099_Start6" name="Vendor proposes a structured multi-week product training program for BuildRight staff, or…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1099_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1099_Task7" name="Training Needs Assessment &amp; Vendor Coordination">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Training Needs Assessment &amp; Vendor Coordination: (a) Category Manager identifies training needs based on: (i) product category knowledge gap survey (quarterly assessment per W51); (ii) low attach rate in companion product sales (e.g., power tool sales without accessory attachment indicates staff not recommending companion products); (iii) high return rates in a category (indicating staff not properly qualifying customer needs); (iv) new product launch requiring specialized knowledge per W564 (NPI &amp; full store rollout); (v) vendor request to increase brand-specific expertise; (b) Category Manager coordinates with vendor training department: (i) defines training scope: product lines to be covered, target knowledge level (basic awareness vs. certified advisor), and target staff count; (ii) agrees on training format: in-store (vendor instructor visits store) vs. regional (staff travel to training venue) vs. online (vendor LMS platform); (iii) establishes certification criteria: assessment method (written test, practical demonstration, or both), passing score, certification validity period (typically 1 year with annual renewal); (iv) negotiates vendor funding: instructor cost, training materials, certification fees, staff incentive program (spiff per certified sale, bonus for certification completion)
Responsible (R): Category Manager
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 4–6 hrs per program design</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1099_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1099_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1099_Task8" name="Staff Nomination &amp; Schedule Coordination">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Staff Nomination &amp; Schedule Coordination: (a) Store Manager nominates staff for the training program based on: (i) department assignment (only staff in relevant sections are eligible); (ii) tenure (minimum 3 months at BuildRight for foundational training, 6 months for advanced certification); (iii) performance (staff with high sales conversion rates prioritized for advanced programs); (iv) schedule availability (training must not create staffing gaps — W34 shift scheduling); (b) HR Training Coordinator registers nominated staff in the training management system: creates cohort per store or region, assigns training schedule (e.g., every Wednesday 2–4 PM for 4 weeks), and sets up assessment schedule; (c) system sends notification to nominated staff: training program overview, schedule, location, required preparation (pre-reading materials from vendor), and certification incentive details; (d) Store Manager adjusts shift schedules per W34 to ensure nominated staff can attend all training sessions without impacting store operations
Responsible (R): Store Manager / HR Training Coordinator
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 2–3 hrs per cohort setup</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1099_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1099_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1099_Task9" name="Training Delivery &amp; Assessment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Training Delivery &amp; Assessment: (a) vendor training specialist delivers the training program: (i) Module 1 (Week 1): Product fundamentals — features, specifications, competitive advantages, target customer profiles; (ii) Module 2 (Week 2): Application scenarios — common customer use cases, project types, companion product recommendations; (iii) Module 3 (Week 3): Hands-on demonstration — staff practice using the products, common issues, troubleshooting; (iv) Module 4 (Week 4): Sales techniques — qualifying customer needs, objection handling, upselling companion products, closing the sale; (v) practical assessments conducted during each module; (b) system tracks attendance and module completion per staff member; (c) at program conclusion: vendor administers certification assessment: (i) written test: product knowledge, specification recall, scenario-based questions; (ii) practical demonstration: staff must correctly demonstrate product features and recommend a complete solution to a role-play customer scenario; (iii) passing score: typically 80% on written + satisfactory on practical; (d) system records assessment results per staff member
Responsible (R): Vendor Training Specialist / HR Training Coordinator
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 2–4 hrs/week × 4 weeks = 8–16 hrs per cohort</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1099_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1099_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1099_Task10" name="Certification Issuance &amp; Recognition">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Certification Issuance &amp; Recognition: (a) for staff who pass the assessment: (i) vendor issues official certification (digital certificate + printed certificate + name badge per W172); (ii) system updates staff profile with certification: vendor name, product category, certification level, issue date, expiry date; (iii) Store Manager recognizes certified staff in store meeting: announces certification, presents badge/certificate, and highlights the certified staff as the &quot;go-to expert&quot; for the product category; (iv) system enables certified staff for higher commission rates on certified product sales (commission differential tracked in payroll per W10); (v) certified staff receive vendor incentive program access: spiffs per certified product sale, quarterly bonus for top sellers, vendor-sponsored prizes for sales contests; (b) for staff who do not pass: (i) system schedules a retake assessment within 30 days; (ii) vendor provides additional coaching materials; (iii) if retake is failed, staff may be nominated for a future cohort
Responsible (R): System / Store Manager
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 30 min per cohort recognition</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1099_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1099_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1099_Task11" name="Certification Maintenance &amp; Annual Renewal">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Certification Maintenance &amp; Annual Renewal: (a) system tracks certification expiry: sends reminder to Store Manager and staff 60 days before expiry; (b) renewal process: (i) annual refresher training (half-day, covering new products and updated specifications); (ii) updated certification assessment; (iii) re-certification upon passing; (c) if certification lapses (staff does not renew within 30 days of expiry): (i) commission rate reverts to standard (non-certified) rate; (ii) staff removed from &quot;certified advisor&quot; recognition; (iii) must complete full training program to re-certify (not just renewal); (d) Category Manager reviews certification program metrics annually: total certified staff per category, sales performance of certified vs. non-certified staff (target: certified staff sell 20–30% more in certified category), vendor ROI (vendor training investment vs. incremental sales), and customer satisfaction scores for certified product categories
Responsible (R): System / Category Manager
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: Annual review: 4–6 hrs</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1099_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1099_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1099_End12" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1099_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
