    <bpmn:process id="W_W1100" name="W1100. Customer Contractor Project Financing &amp; Supplier Credit Line Partnership Management" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: BuildRight&#x27;s B2B contractor customer (trade account) requests extended payment terms or project-specific financing beyond their standard credit limit per W24, or Category Manager proactively offers project financing to high-value contractor accounts during quarterly business review per W617
Frequency: ~25–40 financing applications/month across all stores (targeting the top 20% of BuildRight&#x27;s 5,200 trade accounts by project value)
Volume: 1 financing arrangement per contractor project
Owner: Finance Manager (Treasury / Credit)
Participants: Trade Counter Supervisor, Finance Manager, Partner Bank/Financing Institution, Customer (Contractor), Category Manager
Source: workflow W1100 — Customer Contractor Project Financing &amp; Supplier Credit Line Partnership Management</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1100_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1100_Lane1" name="Trade Counter Supervisor">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1100_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1100_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1100_Lane2" name="Finance Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1100_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1100_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1100_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1100_Lane3" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1100_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1100_End11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1100_Start5" name="BuildRight&#x27;s B2B contractor customer (trade account) requests extended payment terms or…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1100_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1100_Task6" name="Contractor Project Assessment &amp; Financing Need Identification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Contractor Project Assessment &amp; Financing Need Identification: (a) Trade Counter Supervisor identifies a financing opportunity when: (i) a contractor customer requests a material order that exceeds their trade account credit limit per W888; (ii) a contractor discusses a large upcoming project during a quarterly business review per W617; (iii) a contractor explicitly asks about extended payment terms for a specific project; (b) Supervisor conducts preliminary assessment: (i) contractor&#x27;s BuildRight account history: years as customer, annual purchase volume, payment track record (on-time payment rate), current outstanding balance, and existing credit limit utilization; (ii) project details: project type (residential, commercial, government), estimated total project cost, estimated material cost (BuildRight portion), project duration, and project owner/client; (iii) contractor&#x27;s financial capacity: business registration (DTI/SEC), financial statements (if available), and existing bank relationships; (c) if preliminary assessment is positive (good payment history, creditworthy project), Supervisor escalates to Finance Manager
Responsible (R): Trade Counter Supervisor
Accountable (A): Finance Manager
Duration: 15–20 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1100_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1100_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1100_Task7" name="Financing Structure Design &amp; Partner Bank Matching">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Financing Structure Design &amp; Partner Bank Matching: Finance Manager designs the financing structure: (a) Option A — Extended BuildRight Credit: BuildRight extends the contractor&#x27;s credit limit for the specific project with extended terms (Net 90 or Net 120); requires Finance Manager approval and may require additional guarantees (post-dated checks per W1380, personal guarantee of the contractor owner); risk: BuildRight bears the full credit risk; (b) Option B — Partner Bank Project Loan: BuildRight refers the contractor to a partner bank for a project-specific loan; the loan proceeds are restricted to material purchases from BuildRight (tri-party agreement: contractor, bank, BuildRight); bank bears the credit risk; BuildRight earns referral commission and guaranteed material sales; (c) Option C — Supply Chain Finance / Dynamic Discounting: BuildRight&#x27;s treasury per W324 offers early payment discount to the contractor&#x27;s project owner/client — the project owner pays BuildRight directly (bypassing the contractor&#x27;s cash flow); applicable only when the project owner is a known entity (developer, corporation, or government agency); (d) Finance Manager selects the optimal option based on: (i) contractor creditworthiness (good: Option A; moderate: Option B; high-risk: Option B required); (ii) project size (small &lt; PHP 500K: Option A; medium PHP 500K–3M: Option A or B; large &gt; PHP 3M: Option B); (iii) project owner quality (government/corporate: Option C viable; individual homeowner: Option A or B); (e) for Option B: Finance Manager matches contractor to the most suitable partner bank based on: bank&#x27;s construction lending appetite, processing speed, interest rate competitiveness, and geographic coverage
Responsible (R): Finance Manager
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 2–3 hrs per application</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1100_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1100_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1100_Task8" name="Application Processing &amp; Credit Assessment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Application Processing &amp; Credit Assessment: (a) Finance Manager assists contractor with financing application: (i) provides partner bank application form with BuildRight referral code; (ii) helps compile required documents: SEC/DTI registration, mayor&#x27;s permit, BIR registration, latest ITR/financial statements, project contract or purchase order from project owner, BuildRight material quotation per W162, and contractor&#x27;s bank statements (6 months); (iii) for Option A (BuildRight credit): Finance Manager conducts internal credit assessment per W886 (credit scoring) using the contractor&#x27;s BuildRight payment history and financial documents; (b) system generates BuildRight Letter of Intent: confirms material availability, pricing, and delivery capability for the specified project materials — this letter is required by the partner bank as evidence of the project&#x27;s material cost; (c) Finance Manager submits application package to partner bank (for Option B) or to Credit Committee (for Option A); (d) processing timeline: Option A — 3–5 business days (internal); Option B — 5–10 banking days (external)
Responsible (R): Finance Manager
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 1–2 hrs per application</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1100_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1100_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1100_Task9" name="Financing Approval, Documentation &amp; Material Release">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Financing Approval, Documentation &amp; Material Release: (a) upon financing approval: (i) for Option A: Finance Manager issues credit limit extension approval with specific terms; (ii) for Option B: partner bank issues Letter of Credit or loan approval letter specifying: loan amount, interest rate, repayment schedule, and restriction of funds to BuildRight material purchases; (iii) for Option C: tri-party agreement signed by contractor, project owner, and BuildRight; (b) system updates contractor&#x27;s account: (i) credit limit increased for the specific project (ring-fenced); (ii) project-specific pricing per W163 applied; (iii) staged delivery schedule per W164 linked to project milestones; (c) material orders released: system stages the material deliveries according to the project timeline (not all materials released at once — manages BuildRight&#x27;s inventory and the contractor&#x27;s storage burden); (d) billing per financing terms: (i) Option A: invoices generated per delivery with extended payment terms; (ii) Option B: partner bank disburses payment to BuildRight per drawdown schedule aligned with material deliveries; (iii) Option C: project owner pays BuildRight directly per agreed milestone schedule
Responsible (R): Finance Manager / System
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 1–2 hrs per project setup</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1100_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1100_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1100_Task10" name="Monitoring, Collection &amp; Partnership Review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Monitoring, Collection &amp; Partnership Review: (a) system monitors project-level receivables: (i) tracks payment status per invoice against financing terms; (ii) flags overdue payments for Finance Manager action per W890 (collection call execution); (iii) for Option B: monitors bank disbursement schedule vs. material delivery schedule; (b) for project milestone completions: Finance Manager coordinates with contractor for next-stage material release; (c) upon project completion: (i) system reconciles total material delivered vs. financed amount; (ii) final billing and payment settlement; (iii) contractor&#x27;s credit limit restored to standard level; (d) quarterly: Finance Manager reviews partnership performance: (i) total financed project volume; (ii) default rate by financing option; (iii) partner bank responsiveness and approval rates; (iv) BuildRight incremental revenue from project financing vs. non-financed accounts; (v) recommends adjustments to partnership terms or adds/replaces partner banks
Responsible (R): System / Finance Manager
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: Ongoing monitoring: 2–3 hrs/week; Quarterly review: 4–6 hrs</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1100_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1100_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1100_End11" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1100_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1100_Annotation12">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-246 (ensure controlled execution — Vendor Sourcing &amp; Onboarding (PA-03.1).) | - operational: Finance Manager (Treasury / Credit) review and approval gate; operational: periodic reconciliation against source documents
Owner: Finance Manager (Treasury / Credit)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1100_Assoc13" sourceRef="W1100_Annotation12" targetRef="W1100_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1100_Flow14" sourceRef="W1100_Start5" targetRef="W1100_Task6" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1100_Flow15" sourceRef="W1100_Task6" targetRef="W1100_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1100_Flow16" sourceRef="W1100_Task7" targetRef="W1100_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1100_Flow17" sourceRef="W1100_Task8" targetRef="W1100_Task9" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1100_Flow18" sourceRef="W1100_Task9" targetRef="W1100_Task10" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1100_Flow19" sourceRef="W1100_Task10" targetRef="W1100_End11" />
    </bpmn:process>
    <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="W1100_diag">
      <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="W1100_plane" bpmnElement="W_W1100">
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1100_Lane1_di" bpmnElement="W1100_Lane1" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="80" width="1370" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1100_Lane2_di" bpmnElement="W1100_Lane2" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="250" width="1370" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1100_Lane3_di" bpmnElement="W1100_Lane3" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="420" width="1370" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1100_Task6_di" bpmnElement="W1100_Task6"><dc:Bounds x="400" y="125" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1100_Task7_di" bpmnElement="W1100_Task7"><dc:Bounds x="610" y="295" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1100_Task8_di" bpmnElement="W1100_Task8"><dc:Bounds x="820" y="295" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
