    <bpmn:process id="W_W1128" name="W1128. Vendor Catalog New Product Sample Request &amp; In-Store Trial Evaluation" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Vendor introduces new product to BuildRight assortment, or category manager identifies new product opportunity, or vendor submits new product proposal
Frequency: ~200–300 new product evaluations/year (aligns with 5–8% annual SKU growth rate)
Volume: 1–5 sample units per product per evaluation
Owner: Category Manager (HQ)
Participants: Category Manager, Buyer, Department Supervisor (pilot store), Vendor Representative
Source: workflow W1128 — Vendor Catalog New Product Sample Request &amp; In-Store Trial Evaluation</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1128_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1128_Lane1" name="Category Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1128_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1128_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1128_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1128_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1128_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1128_Lane2" name="Department Supervisor">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1128_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1128_End10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1128_Start4" name="Vendor introduces new product to BuildRight assortment, or category manager identifies…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1128_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1128_Task5" name="Sample Request &amp; Vendor Coordination">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Sample Request &amp; Vendor Coordination: (a) Category Manager reviews vendor&#x27;s new product proposal (specs, pricing, margin, target customer segment); (b) if product passes initial desktop review, Category Manager requests physical samples from vendor: 2–5 units for evaluation, plus product documentation (SDS, warranty, installation guide, barcode/GTIN); (c) vendor ships samples to HQ merchandising office; (d) sample receipt logged in ERP with unique evaluation tracking number; (e) evaluation timeline set: 2–4 weeks from sample receipt to decision
Responsible (R): Category Manager
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 15–20 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1128_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1128_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1128_Task6" name="Product Evaluation Committee Review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Product Evaluation Committee Review: (a) Category Manager, Buyer, and relevant Department Supervisor conduct hands-on evaluation: product quality (materials, finish, durability), packaging (shelf appeal, protection during shipping, labeling compliance), compatibility (fits existing planogram section, complementary to current assortment), compliance (Philippine product standards: DTI-BPS ICC mark, fire safety rating for electrical products, FDA registration for household chemicals); (b) pricing analysis: vendor&#x27;s proposed wholesale price vs. target margin, competitive price comparison, promotional funding availability; (c) evaluation scored using standardized scorecard (weighted criteria: quality 30%, margin 25%, customer demand 20%, shelf fit 15%, compliance 10%); (d) recommendation: approve for pilot, approve for direct rollout, defer, or reject
Responsible (R): Category Manager / Buyer
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 30–60 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1128_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1128_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1128_Task7" name="Pilot Store Trial (If Approved for Pilot)">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Pilot Store Trial (If Approved for Pilot): (a) select 5–10 pilot stores across different regions for market test; (b) vendor ships trial quantity to pilot stores (10–20 units per store); (c) Department Supervisor places product on shelf in designated location per planogram guidance; (d) product tagged with &quot;New Product&quot; shelf marker; (e) store staff briefed on product features and key selling points; (f) sales tracked daily via POS for 2–4 week trial period; (g) Department Supervisor collects customer feedback and staff observations
Responsible (R): Department Supervisor (Pilot Stores)
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 2–4 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1128_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1128_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1128_Task8" name="Trial Results Analysis &amp; Go/No-Go Decision">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Trial Results Analysis &amp; Go/No-Go Decision: (a) Category Manager reviews trial data: units sold, sell-through rate, average daily velocity, gross margin, customer returns, staff feedback; (b) compares trial performance against benchmarks (minimum sell-through rate: 60% in 4 weeks for standard items, 40% for premium/specialty); (c) vendor negotiation leverage: strong trial results → better pricing/promotional terms; weak results → price reduction request or pass; (d) final decision: approve full rollout, approve with conditions (price reduction, promotional support), extend pilot, or discontinue; (e) if approved: product enters full assortment, added to replenishment cycle, assigned to planogram, included in next promotional calendar
Responsible (R): Category Manager
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 1–2 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1128_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1128_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1128_Task9" name="Sample Disposition &amp; Record Keeping">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Sample Disposition &amp; Record Keeping: (a) evaluated samples dispositioned: kept as reference/display unit in HQ sample room, donated to community project per W444, or returned to vendor; (b) evaluation record archived in ERP with full scorecard, photos, trial data, and final decision; (c) if product rejected, vendor notified with feedback; (d) if product approved, evaluation record linked to item master creation workflow (W252)
Responsible (R): Category Manager
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 15–20 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1128_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1128_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1128_End10" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1128_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1128_Annotation11">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-246 (ensure controlled execution — Vendor Sourcing &amp; Onboarding (PA-03.1).) | - operational: Category Manager review and approval gate
Owner: Category Manager (HQ)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
