    <bpmn:process id="W_W1145" name="W1145. Vendor Seasonal Import Container Consolidation &amp; Optimization Planning" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Seasonal buy planning cycle (W32) generates import PO projections, or monthly import volume review identifies consolidation opportunity
Frequency: Quarterly planning cycles; monthly execution adjustments
Volume: ~400–600 TEUs/month across ~400 import vendors; consolidation targets 10–15% reduction in container count
Owner: Supply Chain Planning Manager (HQ)
Participants: Supply Chain Planner, Buyer / Category Manager, Import Logistics Coordinator, Vendor Representatives, Freight Forwarder
Source: workflow W1145 — Vendor Seasonal Import Container Consolidation &amp; Optimization Planning</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1145_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1145_Lane1" name="Supply Chain Planner">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1145_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1145_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1145_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1145_Lane2" name="Buyer">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1145_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1145_Lane3" name="Freight Forwarder">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1145_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1145_Lane4" name="Import Logistics Coordinator">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1145_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1145_End12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1145_Start6" name="Seasonal buy planning cycle (W32) generates import PO projections, or monthly import…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1145_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1145_Task7" name="Quarterly Consolidation Opportunity Analysis">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Quarterly Consolidation Opportunity Analysis: (a) at the start of each quarter, Supply Chain Planning Manager extracts projected import PO data from seasonal buy plan (W32) and demand forecast (W31); (b) group projected import volume by country of origin, port of loading, and shipping window; (c) identify consolidation clusters: vendors shipping from same port (e.g., Shenzhen, Shanghai, Keelung) within same 2-week window; (d) calculate current vs. projected container utilization per cluster; (e) quantify consolidation savings: fewer containers × freight per TEU = estimated quarterly savings; (f) prioritize consolidation opportunities by savings potential (top 10 clusters typically represent 60–70% of savings)
Responsible (R): Supply Chain Planner
Accountable (A): Supply Chain Planning Manager
Duration: 1–2 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1145_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1145_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1145_Task8" name="Vendor Coordination &amp; Shipment Scheduling Alignment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Vendor Coordination &amp; Shipment Scheduling Alignment: (a) for each prioritized consolidation cluster, Buyer contacts vendors to align production and shipment schedules; (b) negotiate delivery-to-port windows that allow consolidation (e.g., &quot;Deliver to Shanghai warehouse by week 15 for consolidated sailing week 16&quot;); (c) coordinate with freight forwarder to arrange consolidated booking: single bill of lading per container with multiple vendor shipments; (d) vendors ship to designated freight forwarder warehouse at port of loading for consolidation; (e) system updates import POs with consolidated shipment reference and estimated sailing date
Responsible (R): Buyer / Import Logistics Coordinator
Accountable (A): Supply Chain Planning Manager
Duration: 3–5 days per cluster</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1145_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1145_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1145_Task9" name="Container Loading Optimization &amp; Documentation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Container Loading Optimization &amp; Documentation: (a) freight forwarder receives goods from multiple vendors at consolidation warehouse; (b) forwarder optimizes container loading plan: heavy items (tiles, cement, steel) at bottom, lighter items (tools, hardware, accessories) on top; (c) incompatible materials segregated (hazmat per W699, chemicals separated from food-contact items); (d) container loaded to target 85–90% utilization by volume and weight (max payload per TEU: ~18–20 metric tons); (e) consolidation documentation prepared: combined packing list, house bills of lading per vendor, container manifest; (f) system receives container loading confirmation with actual quantities per vendor PO
Responsible (R): Freight Forwarder / Import Logistics Coordinator
Accountable (A): Supply Chain Planning Manager
Duration: 1–2 days per container</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1145_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1145_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1145_Task10" name="Inbound Tracking &amp; Cost Allocation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Inbound Tracking &amp; Cost Allocation: (a) consolidated container tracked via supply chain control tower (W250) from port of loading to Philippine destination port; (b) upon arrival and customs clearance (W464), container devanned at DC; (c) goods received per individual vendor PO using standard goods receipt process (W3); (d) freight cost allocated proportionally to each vendor&#x27;s PO based on volume/weight share: vendor A occupied 40% of container → vendor A&#x27;s items absorb 40% of freight cost in landed cost calculation (W2B.12); (e) actual consolidation savings tracked: freight cost per unit vs. baseline (non-consolidated) rate
Responsible (R): Import Logistics Coordinator / System
Accountable (A): Supply Chain Planning Manager
Duration: 1 day</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1145_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1145_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1145_Task11" name="Consolidation Performance Review &amp; Savings Reporting">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Consolidation Performance Review &amp; Savings Reporting: (a) monthly consolidation report generated: containers consolidated, utilization rate improvement (target: 70% → 85%), freight savings vs. baseline, vendor compliance rate (vendors meeting consolidation schedule); (b) quarterly review with Category Managers: consolidation savings by category, impact on lead times, vendor feedback; (c) consolidation savings feed into vendor scorecard (W44) as logistics collaboration metric; (d) annual freight cost benchmarking (W762) updated with consolidation data
Responsible (R): Supply Chain Planner
Accountable (A): VP Supply Chain
Duration: 2–3 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1145_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1145_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1145_End12" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1145_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1145_Annotation13">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-246 (ensure controlled execution — Vendor Sourcing &amp; Onboarding (PA-03.1).) | - operational: Supply Chain Planning Manager review and approval gate
Owner: Supply Chain Planning Manager (HQ)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1145_Assoc14" sourceRef="W1145_Annotation13" targetRef="W1145_Start6" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1145_Flow15" sourceRef="W1145_Start6" targetRef="W1145_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1145_Flow16" sourceRef="W1145_Task7" targetRef="W1145_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1145_Flow17" sourceRef="W1145_Task8" targetRef="W1145_Task9" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1145_Flow18" sourceRef="W1145_Task9" targetRef="W1145_Task10" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1145_Flow19" sourceRef="W1145_Task10" targetRef="W1145_Task11" />
